 "notes": "New shelf (no old data). Archetypes are named key materials; versions only where the source page gives them (origins, trade names, landmark perfumes). Rose otto/absolute kept as raw materials; the attar-style rose oil and Taif rose live on the Attar shelf (cross-link). Grasse tradition already on another shelf, so no traditions here. Left out: jasmine, ylang-ylang and tuberose absolutes and orris irone details (no page retrieved in time; wiki API rate-limited); Lilial (banned for fertility harm, not a current hobby material); Sclareol (ambroxide precursor, rarely owned); synthetic-musk class beyond Galaxolide/Muscone; Kao and Pfizer brand entries (not fragrance-house pages); Pell Wall kit names and Perfumer's Apprentice founding year (snippet-only). Hedione year 1962 = end of Demole's 1957–62 synthesis work."
